Read the bounded server/core log buffer

Usage: xrm logs [OPTIONS]

OPTIONS:
  -h,   --help            Show this help message 
        --cursor CURSOR   Transport buffer cursor, not a log record number; 0 
                          starts at the oldest available chunk Default: 0. 
        --limit LIMIT     Maximum log text bytes returned by this read 
                          (default 65536) Default: 65536. 

GLOBAL OPTIONS (before the command):
        --socket PATH     xrmd Unix domain socket 
        --json            Write machine readable output 
        --verbose         Include original diagnostics in human errors 

Examples:
  xrm logs --limit 100
